A||N||26||Standard||Need advice on fiero's!||||1||
Z||000000||Standard||01-18-2000||01:13 AM||||Alright guys, i've been looking around for a v6 fiero for awhile and now I've found 2! I need to choose between an 86 SE 4spd and an 86.5 GT 5spd.<BR>86 SE - 116,000 PW, PL, Sunroof, Performance sound, clutch was replace (he doens't know when) black/gray, luggage rack.. wants 1500 for it.<P>86.5 GT - this is what he told me-<BR>Hi Mike, here is the info on the GT's, I will be reasonable on the prices as I will be moving and need to sell them. <P>'86 GT, 5-speed (one of 2000 built in '86.) 142,000. PW,PM,PL, AC, sunroof, rear defrost. Black with grey effects. Bought from original<BR>owner in June. Both tailights are good, no cracks on them. One sail panel needs replacing, other one is decent. Never in a crash.<P>What this car needs: Paint, new decklid (could be fixed but wing was  ripped off before I got it) Driver seat is ripped, can be covered. Dash has corner wear. Needs right ground effect. Needs a interior cleaning.<BR>The clutch seems fine though I noticed when shifting in 3rd it grinds  a little, needs adjusting. Needs front manifold. Suspension is decent.<BR>I have the original papers for this car and good title. Tires good.<BR>He wants $1400.<P>any advice?  TIA!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||01-18-2000||01:26 AM||||Make him a deal on both!!<P>"Buy one get one half off" ??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||Standard||01-18-2000||01:32 AM||||Should have clarified a little, it's two different guys.  One lives kind of close to me, the other is about an hour away. grrr.. <B>i want a v6!!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||01-18-2000||01:43 AM||||Prices on these cars seem to be a little higher out here (SF, CA)  I looked at a 85GT yesterday 113,000 on the dial. he wants $2,500 for the car, I looked at it and walked(FAST)away. It looked like trash. Body damage, interior & upholstery was.....I can't even say the words. Exhaust mainfold leak (bad)crack, one eye open one eye missing, needed paint bad, sails crack. I don't know what this guy was thinking. He knew that he didn't have a sale when I drove up in my fresh wash and waxed black 86SE (same as his 85GT) He didn't have much to say to me. So as I left I light em up and waved....see ya   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 01-18-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000004||ChadMan||01-18-2000||09:26 AM||||You're gonna have to drive 'em, obviously, but unless you're hooked on the fastbacks, the SE sounds like the better buy, because of:<P>-Fewer miles<BR>-Newer clutch<BR>-Possible bad 3rd gear synchro in GT (and Getrags cost $$$ to fix!)<BR>-Body work needed on GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||01-18-2000||02:58 PM||||I like the lower mileage, but I also forgot to mention that the GT had it's clutch replaced in '98.  Right now I am leaning towards the SE tho, I gotta call the guy up. I'll let everyone know how it goes.  thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shiner||01-18-2000||04:19 PM||||I have a bad synchro on my 3rd gear too. ('87 GT)  How much are you thinking this is going to cost to get fixed?<p>[This message has been edited by Shiner (edited 01-18-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000007||Tom88gt||01-19-2000||01:01 PM||||Without you personnally inspecting both cars it's hard to say.  But I would vote for the 86.5  I think there was a mid-year upgrade for 1986 to the Gertrag 5 speed.  Maybe some other stuff as well.  Check out the "fireo trend internet magazine", don't know the address, try a web search.  Lots of good year by year info, and notes on the 86.5||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||01-19-2000||03:11 PM||||It is the 5spd, which is the main reason I want it.. how much longer do you guys think it would last?  It already has 142,000 miles on it..||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tom88gt||01-19-2000||05:24 PM||||After 10 years/100,000mi.....I care a lot more about the care it received than the miles.  <P>By comparison, I bought my 85 Volvo from the original owner.  The maintenance booklet has every service interval formally stamped by Volvo dealers or independant Volvo shops.  It has 180,000mi and is in better condition mechanical/interior/body than many Jap/US cars with half the years and miles that I've seen.<P>That said, better to buy the model you want and spend a few $$ bringing it back up to speed than to buy a model you didn't quite want because it was a little "nicer".  If the cars are fairly close in overall condition, buy the one you will love the most down the road.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||01-20-2000||12:32 AM||||good points.  Right now I'm at the point where whoever contacts me first is the one I'll probably buy.  I haven't heard from the guy with the SE since last thursday and I e-mailed the guy with the GT this afternoon...  <P>I was looking through my Chilton's for info on the getrag 5spd, and it lists a 1st/2nd synchro, 3rd/4th synchro, and 5th synchro.  So if the synchro was going wouldn't 4th grind too?  or do I just not know enough?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||01-20-2000||08:32 PM||||You can never know enough.  That's all I have to say about that.||||reg||1
Z||000012||lowCG||01-21-2000||06:16 PM||||I would go for any acceptable deal on any car that has a V6 5spd,and is in good shape cosmetically.But that's just me.<BR>Don't rush it,there are a lot out there,even if you have to drive a day or so to look.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Eddie.H||01-21-2000||09:18 PM||||A GT in NJ YOU could get a nice one for 1500 1700. 1400 needs that much work youll put 1500 into in the frist year shop around dont do what I did take your time and shop shop shop around it will come to you good luck guy EDDIE||||reg||4
Z||000014||fieroshop||01-21-2000||10:30 PM||||Well I see that you are getting a lot af advice as to what car you should get and also that they can buy a GT back esat for very litle money. Problem with the eastern Fieros is that a lot of them are full of rust. So far I have two customers that went back east and bought their GT's back there and drove back to Calif. They would have been better off buying one here for a little more money and saved themselves at least $2000.00 plus the drive and fuel and hotel stays. Just my $0.02 worth.||||reg||8
Z||000015||BigBoyToys||01-21-2000||11:29 PM||||Fieroshop, Great point! I hd been looking for a Fiero GT for years here in the NE and could not find one that the inside rear quarters you couldn't put your finger thru. Finally looked at one that a kid in the navy bought in California and brought back east when he got out, he had run it one winter and was still solid. Even got the Cali Title. So I finally got a solid GT with some of the typical problems (pickup coil kept leaving him stranded) so I picked it up for a mear 1700$. Also mechanic around here won't touch them because of the fear of working with every bolt either froze up or crumbling. The moral is patience and look them over very carfully from underneath, get rite up in there with a flashlight if need be. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Standard||01-24-2000||03:17 AM||||I looked at the 86.5 GT today.  Not in tip-top shape but not too bad.  The tags on it are from 97 so it's been sitting awhile.  Dead battery, tried to jump it with his other Fiero but it wouldn't start.  Noticed the turn signal stalk was good and broke.  The lace wheels are in pretty good shape.  New front tires.  Both of the taillights are perfect.  Body is straight.  If I can get him down to $1000 do ya think I should take it? considering I could part it out after that and make money off of it... but <B>don't worry</B>, I wouldn't do that.  I wanna V6||||reg||5
Z||000017||Tom88gt||01-24-2000||07:57 AM||||Sounds good!  Offer a thou  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  If he doesn't take it, leave your number.  It doesn't sound like anyone is beating down his door, except you.||||reg||6
Z||000018||mshill||01-24-2000||04:55 PM||||Standard,  I still don't feel that any care that won't start and is not registered, is not worth more than $500.  You have no idea what else could be mechanically wrong with it. Offer $500 and leave your phone number.  It'll be around for a while unless the guy figures out how to get it started so someone can road test it.||||reg||13
Z||000019||DRH||01-24-2000||05:50 PM||||I agree with mshill. It's been sitting 2 years... There must have been something wrong to park it in the first place... If it won't start you have NO idea what is wrong...<P>It sounds like you will have to go into the trans... 142K and 2 years +/- sitting is not a good combo, you may need to rebuild the engine soon (if it is not already shot)...<P>On a MN car, CHECK FOR RUST!!! If the space frame is too far gone it may already be a parts car!<P>Ultimately it is up to you though. If you REALLY like it and are willing to take the risk, maybe it IS worth it to YOU.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 01-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Standard||01-25-2000||12:24 AM||||I agree with both of you, too.  Before I give him any money I'm gonna take the batt. out of my Fiero and throw it in there.  If it starts I'm gonna drive it around for at least an hour, check everything out, etc...  since I just got pip I'll post pics of it.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PlanteGT.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PlanteGT2.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||1
