Z||000022||M King||01-25-2000||12:48 PM||||LOL, I would have to agree with you chadman.<p>[This message has been edited by M King (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000023||Tom88gt||01-25-2000||12:59 PM||||mshill pick up on a good point.  I didn't notice that you said it didn't run and was sitting for a couple of years.  <P>$500 is probably more appropriate.  I recently picked up an 88 formula t-top that quit running and couldn't get it started.  But it looked clean enough otherwise that it was worth a shot as the price was cut in half by the seller before I called.  Runs pretty good now and I'm happy with it.  But it was a gamble.<P>The photo looks pretty good.  Low ball the seller and let him decide.  If he thinks it's worth more, let him get it running, inspected, titled and it may be worth his asking price.  But if he's not willing to get the car "ready for sale" then he knows it's not worth what he's asking and you probably don't have any other buyers competing anyway.||||reg||6
