Z||000025||Standard||02-01-2000||02:07 AM||||Finally got a call back from the guy with the GT.  Said he got it started, and he'll take 1200 for it and he'll throw in a bra.  I'm going up there this weekend to test drive it.  Anything specific I should look for on a car with 142,000 miles?  <P>I'm also planning to rebuild the engine in the fall no matter what.  even if it had half the miles on it.  I'm gonna take engine rebuilding/machining courses at the Tech school so it gives me an engine to rebuild.. how about a stroke and bore? 3.2 litre.. hehehe<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 02-01-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000026||batboy||02-01-2000||07:29 AM||||Seems like with high miles, the inner tie rods and sometimes the ball joints get a little wear (sloppy steering and handling). Check out all the electrical stuff, especially the headlights. Good luck.||||reg||1
